.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_GROUP_TO_NAME 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_group_to_name
.Nd get name of group
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft const char *
.Fo SSL_group_to_name
.Fa "SSL *ssl"
.Fa "int id"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_group_to_name
is used to retrieve the TLS group name associated with a given TLS group
ID, as registered via built-in or external providers and as returned by
a call to
.Xr SSL_get1_groups 3
or
.Xr SSL_get_shared_group 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
If non-NULL,
.Fn SSL_group_to_name
returns the TLS group name corresponding to the given
.Fa id
as a NUL-terminated string.
If
.Fn SSL_group_to_name
returns NULL, an error occurred; possibly no corresponding tlsname was
registered during provider initialisation.
.Pp
Note that the return value is valid only during the lifetime of the SSL
object
.Fa ssl .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssl 7
